@page "/Account/Manage/ProfilePhoto"

<!--
THESIS: Profile-photo management is the account hall's portrait station for reviewing and replacing the member avatar.
OWN-WORLD: A flat working sheet, a two-stop route, a circular portrait field, and one teal save action.
STORY: The member sees the purpose of the avatar, chooses a replacement, frames it, and returns to account management.
FIRST VIEWPORT: The Profile photo heading and current-photo context lead directly into the shared editor.
FORM: One focused portrait workspace inside the static-SSR ManageLayout; only the editor remains an InteractiveAuto island.
-->

<PageTitle>Profile photo</PageTitle>

<div class="manage-photo">
    <header class="manage-photo-heading">
        <h1>Profile photo</h1>
        <p>
            Update the photo used for your Nova avatar. Choose a new image, frame it,
            and save when it looks right.
        </p>
    </header>

    <ProfilePhotoEditor ReturnUrl="/Account/Manage" CancelUrl="/Account/Manage" @rendermode="InteractiveAuto" />
</div>
